    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0414" n="278" xml:id="pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a/392a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-12T17:00:00-05:00">November 12, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>294. The Secretary of State handed the Japanese Ambassador an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> this noon concerning the Japanese
                    desires at the forthcoming naval conference which reads as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> printed
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>You may communicate a copy of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to
                    the Prime Minister for his confidential information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
